{"kind":"artifact","text":"The architecture reference states the admitted-time authority rule and the boundary on what the browser may derive, carried into the plain-language rewrite now in main. Exact clean pushed head 93f0b2a6fe2431b42dc38fbd2a03cd65132f0b3e on request/decision-records-ui-recut; local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash 1f7e7907, checkout clean. Filed under planner's repair child ae0d3d86 and my promise 1abf201b.\n\nTHE NON-MECHANICAL PART OF THE RECUT, restated because it is what a reviewer must judge. My own rewrite of this page merged first as main d8edc000a, and this lane's page was written against the version before it. Both describe the same layers. I checked whether the rewrite had absorbed this lane's material and it had not: \"Layer 5 and layer 7\", \"what the browser may derive\", \"keep-decision-records.md\" and \"satisfier\" were all absent from main's page. Resolving to either side would have lost something real, so I carried the lane's material into the rewritten page by hand. The result is 1184 lines: main's 1093-line rewrite intact plus 92 added lines, with a single deletion, the ui/ table row this head deliberately extends. Front matter is byte-identical to main and no citation was added, removed or re-anchored.\n\nWHAT THE ADDED MATERIAL SAYS. The admitted-time authority rule: a ratification is decided by the satisfier on the target kind's definition as it stood when the target statement was admitted, never by whichever definition governs now — the rule lifecycle already follows, for the same reason. And the layer 5 to layer 7 boundary: layer 7 may read any field layer 5 projects and combine those fields for presentation, but may not name a relation layer 5 does not project and then treat it as a fact about the workroom. Adoption is the worked case.\n\nONE PASSAGE THIS LANE RELIES ON AND DID NOT WRITE. The page already states, at the live-membership boundary, that \"A departed actor may still supersede an earlier act they authored; that narrow cleanup exception confers no force on a new state or on a ratification.\" That sentence is load-bearing for the repair at b35454ba: it is why withdraw is deliberately outside the participant predicate while publish is inside it. I had earlier described departed-author withdraw as a false offer, contradicting this page; codex caught it and the page was right. Planner's ba9326ae carries the same wrong premise, which I recorded at f1fb9be4.\n\nTHREE THINGS NOT CARRIED VERBATIM, reported rather than applied silently. The lane's page contained \"This paragraph previously stated the live-vocabulary rule, and the browser implemented it\". That is false of main's page: it refers to head 3fd75543, which git merge-base --is-ancestor shows is an ancestor of neither main nor the merge-base — an abandoned draft. Carrying it would have put a false claim about the page's own history into the reference, so I rewrote the opening as \"The hazard is not only a coding error\" and kept every normative claim, including \"Layer 7 derives no authority of its own\". The other two are spellings, serialisation to serialization and \"for ever\" to forever, matching main's consistently American page.\n\nTHE PAGE IS UNCHANGED SINCE THE PREVIOUS HEAD; the commit moved because its Rests-On trailer now names ae0d3d86 rather than parent d14e96fb alone. Tree hash 1f7e7907 is identical to the retired 8ad3c0c2.\n\nWHY THIS RESTS ON THE BEHAVIOUR ARTIFACTS. A documentation artifact resting only on the promise can never be flared by a change to the thing it describes. This one rests on internal/workroom 352f2b96, ui b35454ba and internal/app 53131ac4, so when that behaviour is succeeded this page is told.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 32 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 33 packages, zero failures and zero cached — which matters here because the docset gate caches past documentation edits and a cached pass would predate this change; gofmt -l . empty; go build and go vet exit 0 with no output; npm test 99/99; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"93f0b2a6fe2431b42dc38fbd2a03cd65132f0b3e","path":"docs/reference/architecture.md"}}